From 041edcea2ca71e554d3aa71edd766a426051e99f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NuoFang6 <991921514@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:42:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf: use exact netlink sock-diag lookup for process
 resolution

resolveSocketByNetlink used NLM_F_DUMP: the kernel ignores the request
id in dump mode and returns every socket, then userspace filters
linearly -- O(all sockets) per connection (measured +1.3ms/conn on
Android with thousands of sockets). Switch to an exact lookup carrying
the full four-tuple (src and dst) in the idiag id: kernel hashes,
userspace gets one message. Measured tcp-lat p50 3.8ms -> 1.9ms with
find-process-mode: strict; strict overhead now +0.4ms vs off.

FindProcessName gains dstIP/dstPort (tunnel passes metadata.DstIP /
DstPort); other platforms accept and ignore them.
---
 component/process/process.go               |  4 ++--
 component/process/process_darwin.go        |  4 +++-
 component/process/process_freebsd_amd64.go |  4 +++-
 component/process/process_linux.go         | 15 +++++++++++----
 component/process/process_other.go         |  4 +++-
 component/process/process_windows.go       |  4 +++-
 tunnel/tunnel.go                           |  2 +-
 7 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/component/process/process.go b/component/process/process.go
index 464f5a79..14fddb41 100644
--- a/component/process/process.go
+++ b/component/process/process.go
@@ -18,8 +18,8 @@ const (
 	UDP = "udp"
 )
 
-func FindProcessName(network string, srcIP netip.Addr, srcPort int) (uint32, string, error) {
-	return findProcessName(network, srcIP, srcPort)
+func FindProcessName(network string, srcIP netip.Addr, srcPort int, dstIP netip.Addr, dstPort int) (uint32, string, error) {
+	return findProcessName(network, srcIP, srcPort, dstIP, dstPort)
 }
 
